2019,"disposition":"not in conflict; Adopted by the CCB","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga47_2019__ci17.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga47_2019__ci17.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:7-2--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga47_2019__ci17.md:occ-6729dc24b827","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga47_2019__ci17.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga47_2019__ci17.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga47_2019__ci17.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"This overture proposed amending multiple BCO provisions to allow individual sessions to decide locally whether women may serve as deacons; the CCB found it not in conflict."}},{"id":"bco:7-2--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga45_2017__ci03.md","record_id":"ccb_advice:inquiries/ga45_2017__ci03.md","type":"CCB advice","title":"Sabbaticals for Officers in the Church","year":2017,"disposition":"in conflict","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga45_2017__ci03.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga45_2017__ci03.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:7-2--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga45_2017__ci03.md:occ-39f548d714c0","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga45_2017__ci03.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga45_2017__ci03.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga45_2017__ci03.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"The proposed overture was in conflict because its use of 'officer' was broader than the definition of ruling elders and deacons in BCO 7-2."}},{"id":"bco:7-2--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga38_2010__ci04.md","record_id":"ccb_advice:inquiries/ga38_2010__ci04.md","type":"CCB advice","title":"Unordained Men and Women Carrying Out Diaconal Ministry","year":2010,"disposition":"in conflict","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga38_2010__ci04.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga38_2010__ci04.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:7-2--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga38_2010__ci04.md:occ-fcfb3f50ced1","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga38_2010__ci04.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga38_2010__ci04.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga38_2010__ci04.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"CCB found an overture appointing unordained persons to diaconal ministry in conflict with the Constitution, including because it implied an unordained office contrary to BCO 17-1."}},{"id":"bco:7-2--inquiry:inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Whether \"Inactive Elders\" or Ruling Elders Elected at a Different Church May Serve as Commissioners at General Assembly","year":2014,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:7-2--inquiry:inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.md:occ-b2a9a70dabf4","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"A rotating-session inactive elder may be elected GA commissioner, but a ruling elder never elected in that congregation may not serve as its commissioner."}},{"id":"bco:7-2--inquiry:inquiries/ga23_1995__ci03.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga23_1995__ci03.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Ordination of candidate with exceptions to six-day creation and male-only office","year":1995,"disposition":"response approved as satisfactory","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga23_1995__ci03.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga23_1995__ci03.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:7-2--inquiry:inquiries/ga23_1995__ci03.md:occ-e63ff4833e4a","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga23_1995__ci03.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga23_1995__ci03.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga23_1995__ci03.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"New River Presbytery's response to prior exceptions was found satisfactory by the GA, though the Review Committee urged the presbytery not to approve future candidates whose exceptions deny fundamentals such as six-day creation or male-only ordination."}},{"id":"bco:7-2--inquiry:inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Ordination of men who believe women may serve as deacons","year":1984,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:7-2--inquiry:inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.md:occ-dd3acee74a24","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"Believing Scripture permits women deacons, while agreeing to abide by BCO standards in practice, is not by itself sufficient grounds to deny ordination or reception in the PCA."}},{"id":"bco:7-2--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Wilson et al. v. Pacific Northwest Presbytery","year":2023,"disposition":"dismissed","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:7-2--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md:occ-fd20bd2a76d4","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.html","repository_path":"cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":475},"excerpt":"…nominated and elected an officer is suspended on the condition of being male (BCO 7-2; 24- 1); the right not to testify against someone is suspended on the condition of being his/her spouse (BCO 35-2); etc. Nor would it have been appropriate for BCO 6-4 to…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["congregational meeting","minor communicant suffrage","voting rights","communing members","church bylaws","BCO 43-1 justiciability","associate pastor resignation","Covenant Presbyterian Church","Pacific Northwest Presbytery"],"standard_of_review":"not_reached","case_numbers":["2022-20"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Members challenged a voting restriction imposed at a congregational meeting. The SJC dismissed the complaint as judicially out of order because BCO 43-1 permits complaints against acts or decisions of church courts, and a congregation is not such a court. It identified other possible routes through a report to Presbytery or review of church records. The adopted decision did not decide whether the voting restriction was constitutionally valid."}},{"id":"bco:7-2--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"David Kniseley et al. v. Rocky Mountain Presbytery","year":2009,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:7-2--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md:occ-52baf089112b","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":155},"excerpt":"…not be construed or interpreted in any way as a weakening of or deviation from BCO 7-2, which states \"[i]n accord with Scripture, these offices [elder and deacon] are open to men only.\"","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["minister title","non-ordained staff","women","constitutional interpretation","presbytery judgment"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2007-13"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"On complaint from TE David Kniseley and others, the SJC reviewed Rocky Mountain Presbytery's refusal to forbid a mission church from giving an unordained female staff member the title 'Minister of Church Life.' The SJC denied the complaint. It held the BCO uses 'minister' synonymously with pastor and teaching elder, but is silent on general use for non-ordained staff; a lower court may exercise discretion subject to BCO 40-2(3)'s WESP review. The decision addressed only the constitutional issue, not the title's wisdom or propriety; four commissioners dissented."}},{"id":"bco:7-2--case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Mark Grasso et al. v. Philadelphia Presbytery","year":2009,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:7-2--case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md:occ-b2f72b262c6d","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":37},"excerpt":"…of Faith and the BCO including a difference regarding the office of deacon (BCO 7.2). Mr. Hsu stated as follows:","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md"},{"id":"bco:7-2--case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md:occ-7c55da5eb5e7","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":41},"excerpt":"…the office of deacon is not one of authority or teaching, but of service, (BCO 7.2) these biblical injunctions do not apply to women holding the office of deacon.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md"},{"id":"bco:7-2--case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md:occ-37f6e3728a12","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":181},"excerpt":"…of whether women may be ordained to the office of deacon. They may not. (BCO 7-2, 9-3). Since the candidate expressed his willingness to operate in accordance with that form of government, the Presbytery did not err in its decision to license him.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md"},{"id":"bco:7-2--case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md:occ-42ed71279827","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":246},"excerpt":"…of whether women may be ordained to the office of deacon. They may not (BCO 7- 2, 9-3). The candidate in this case expressed his willingness to operate in accordance with that form of government, and we find no reason in the record of the case not to…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md"},{"id":"bco:7-2--case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md:occ-645623dfa31f","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":272},"excerpt":"…not be construed or interpreted in any way as a weakening of or deviation from BCO 7-2, which states \"[i]n accord with Scripture, these offices [elder and deacon] are open to men only.\"","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["ordination","licensure","women deacons","stated difference","confessional subscription"],"case_numbers":["2008-1"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The Session of Crossroads Community Church challenged Philadelphia Presbytery's licensing and ordination of a candidate who stated a difference concerning women and the office of deacon but agreed to follow the BCO. The SJC denied the complaint and affirmed Presbytery's judgment; a dissent argued it should have been sustained."}},{"id":"bco:7-2--case:cases/ga20_1992__1991-04.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga20_1992__1991-04.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Robert D. Hopper v. James River Presbytery","year":1992,"disposition":"","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga20_1992__1991-04.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga20_1992__1991-04.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:7-2--case:cases/ga20_1992__1991-04.md:occ-c8258550d7ae","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga20_1992__1991-04.html","repository_path":"cases/ga20_1992__1991-04.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":856},"excerpt":"* BCO 7-2 dealing with officers in the Church necessarily being male, and TE Hopper's view that WOMEN OUGHT TO BE ALLOWED TO PROPHESY IN PUBLIC WORSHIP, such women being permitted to bring a \"counsel of encouragement to the congregation\";","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga20_1992__1991-04.md"},{"id":"bco:7-2--case:cases/ga20_1992__1991-04.md:occ-fb64522d6640","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga20_1992__1991-04.html","repository_path":"cases/ga20_1992__1991-04.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":858},"excerpt":"* BCO 7-2 stating that the \"ordinary and perpetual classes of office in the Church are elders and deacons\" and the establishment of a de facto third office in the Church, the office of \"prophet\";","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga20_1992__1991-04.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1991-4"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The SJC denied Hopper's complaint against James River Presbytery's April 13, 1991 order barring him from teaching or preaching his views on prophecy and tongues. It rejected all five specifications: Scripture did not forbid the order; the 1974 Pastoral Letter did not address presbytery's power to enjoin such teaching; forbearance did not preclude protecting peace and purity; presbytery could restrict preaching short of a heresy finding without binding conscience; and allowing presbyteral discussion while restricting congregational teaching was not inconsistent. The action remained in force."}},{"id":"bco:7-2--case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-04.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-04.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Chappell v. Eastern Carolina Presbytery","year":1991,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga19_1991__1990-04.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga19_1991__1990-04.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:7-2--case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-04.md:occ-b523944188cb","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga19_1991__1990-04.html","repository_path":"cases/ga19_1991__1990-04.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":519},"excerpt":"6. BCO 7-2 The Elders jointly have the government and spiritual oversight of the Church, including teaching.","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga19_1991__1990-04.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["presbytery commission powers","Session Pro Tem","suspension of session without due process","limited jurisdiction of church courts","ministerial and declarative power","congregational right to choose officers","ecclesiastical versus civil power","Fuller Memorial Presbyterian Church","delegation of sessional duties","complaint","ruling elder","presbytery action"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1990-4"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Ruling Elder Chappell complained against Eastern Carolina Presbytery's Commission, which had suspended the session of Fuller Memorial Presbyterian Church and constituted itself as a 'Session Pro Tem' without due process or congregational consent. The SJC sustained the complaint, holding that the BCO grants no authority for a presbytery to depose a session and act in its place, that suspension requires due process, and that the congregation has an inalienable right to be governed by officers it has chosen."}},{"id":"bco:7-2--overture:ga51_2024:15","record_id":"overture:ga51_2024:15","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 7-2 to Specify Ordination for Biological Males Only","year":2024,"disposition":"Answered in the negative","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga51_2024.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga51_2024.md","evidence_basis":"overture_action_target","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:7-2--overture:ga51_2024:15:occ-eb5e54348737","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga51_2024.html#ga51-p1277","repository_path":"markdown/ga51_2024.md#ga51-p1277","locator":{"fragment":"ga51-p1277","page":1277},"excerpt":"Amend BCO 7-2 to Specify Ordination for Biological Males Only","sources":["disposition_bco,title_subject"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga51_2024.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"source":"the Session of West End Presbyterian Church, (to CCB, OC)"}},{"id":"bco:7-2--overture:ga38_2010:10","record_id":"overture:ga38_2010:10","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 1-4, 4-2, 5-10, 7-2, 9-2, 9-7 and Add BCO 9-8 for Unordained Diaconal Ministry","year":2010,"disposition":"Answered in the negative","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga38_2010.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga38_2010.md","evidence_basis":"overture_action_target","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:7-2--overture:ga38_2010:10:occ-7c8ef248a1b5","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga38_2010.html#ga38-p394","repository_path":"markdown/ga38_2010.md#ga38-p394"